cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "polyreflexion: recursive Sierpinski reflexion with a polycontextural meta layer"
abstract: >-
  A recursive text-reflexion engine over a Sierpinski triangle of three
  perspectives, steered by a polycontextural meta layer that judges each cycle
  from subjective, objective and dialectical contexts and selects the next
  recursion move. Ships the OpenToM and GPQA Diamond evaluation suites used to
  measure it.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/gaialogicag/polyreflexion"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-22"
keywords:
  - large language models
  - self-reflection
  - recursive reasoning
  - theory of mind
  - polycontexturality
authors:
